  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Numbers",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 20,
    "summary": "Miriam dies—Moses smites a rock at Meribah and brings forth water—The king of Edom refuses to let Israel pass peacefully through his land—Aaron dies, and Eleazar becomes the high priest.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Then came the children of Israel, even the whole congregation, into the desert of Zin in the first month: and the people abode in Kadesh; and Miriam died there, and was buried there.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 130,
            "end": 136,
            "text": "Num. 27:14 (12–14); 33:36."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:1",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And there was no water for the congregation: and they gathered themselves together against Moses and against Aaron.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:2",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And the people chode with Moses, and spake, saying, Would God that we had died when our brethren died before the Lord!",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "OR contended (also v. 13, for “strove”). Deut. 33:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:3",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And why have ye brought up the congregation of the Lord into this wilderness, that we and our cattle should die there?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:4",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And wherefore have ye made us to come up out of Egypt, to bring us in unto this evil place? it is no place of seed, or of figs, or of vines, or of pomegranates; neither is there any water to drink.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 97
          },
          {
            "start": 169,
            "end": 171
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:5",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses and Aaron went from the presence of the assembly unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and they fell upon their faces: and the glory of the Lord appeared unto them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 110,
            "text": "HEB tent of meeting."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:6",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Lord spake unto Moses, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:7",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Take the rod, and gather thou the assembly together, thou, and Aaron thy brother, and speak ye unto the rock before their eyes; and it shall give forth his water, and thou shalt bring forth to them water out of the rock: so thou shalt give the congregation and their beasts drink.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "See JST Gen. 50:34 (Appendix). Ex. 4:20."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "Ex. 17:6 (6–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:8",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses took the rod from before the Lord, as he commanded him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:9",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses and Aaron gathered the congregation together before the rock, and he said unto them, Hear now, ye rebels; must we fetch you water out of this rock?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "Ps. 106:33."
          },
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "TG Rashness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
