        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "This is the water of Meribah; because the children of Israel strove with the Lord, and he was sanctified in them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "IE Quarrel, Strife, Contention. Ex. 17:7; Deut. 33:8; Ezek. 47:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Ezek. 48:28. TG Strife."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:13",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses sent messengers from Kadesh unto the king of Edom, Thus saith thy brother Israel, Thou knowest all the travail that hath befallen us:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Judg. 11:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Judg. 11:17.",
            "prettyString": "Judges 11:17",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "judges",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 11,
                    "end": 11,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 17,
                        "end": 17
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:14",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "How our fathers went down into Egypt, and we have dwelt in Egypt a long time; and the Egyptians vexed us, and our fathers:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:15",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And when we cried unto the Lord, he heard our voice, and sent an angel, and hath brought us forth out of Egypt: and, behold, we are in Kadesh, a city in the uttermost of thy border:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "Ex. 32:34. TG Angels."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 131
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:16",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "Let us pass, I pray thee, through thy country: we will not pass through the fields, or through the vineyards, neither will we drink of the water of the wells: we will go by the king’s high way, we will not turn to the right hand nor to the left, until we have passed thy borders.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 134
          },
          {
            "start": 184,
            "end": 188
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:17",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And Edom said unto him, Thou shalt not pass by me, lest I come out against thee with the sword.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "HEB through me (i.e., through my land)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:18",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And the children of Israel said unto him, We will go by the high way: and if I and my cattle drink of thy water, then I will pay for it: I will only, without doing any thing else, go through on my feet.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "Deut. 2:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 163
          },
          {
            "start": 174,
            "end": 179
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Deut. 2:28.",
            "prettyString": "Deuteronomy 2:28",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "deuteronomy",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 2,
                    "end": 2,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 28,
                        "end": 28
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:19",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said, Thou shalt not go through. And Edom came out against him with much people, and with a strong hand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:20",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Thus Edom refused to give Israel passage through his border: wherefore Israel turned away from him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:21",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And the children of Israel, even the whole congregation, journeyed from Kadesh, and came unto mount Hor.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:22",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Lord spake unto Moses and Aaron in mount Hor, by the coast of the land of Edom, saying,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "HEB border."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:23",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "Aaron shall be gathered unto his people: for he shall not enter into the land which I have given unto the children of Israel, because ye rebelled against my word at the water of Meribah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 137,
            "end": 145,
            "text": "TG Rebellion."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Rebellion.",
            "prettyString": "TG Rebellion",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Rebellion",
                "entryId": "tg-rebellion",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:24",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "Take Aaron and Eleazar his son, and bring them up unto mount Hor:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:25",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And strip Aaron of his garments, and put them upon Eleazar his son: and Aaron shall be gathered unto his people, and shall die there.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 112
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:26",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses did as the Lord commanded: and they went up into mount Hor in the sight of all the congregation.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:27",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses stripped Aaron of his garments, and put them upon Eleazar his son; and Aaron died there in the top of the mount: and Moses and Eleazar came down from the mount.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Num. 33:38 (37–39); Deut. 10:6; 32:50."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 20:28",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "And when all the congregation saw that Aaron was dead, they mourned for Aaron thirty days, even all the house of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [],
